Rachel Elizabeth Dillon <rac...@akrasiac.org> wrote:

> the endgame is really a cakewalk

That might be the wrong perspective.

Instead, think of it as: the endgame
is known to be _so stinking hard_ that
everyone grossly over-prepares, purely
to _make_ it into a cakewalk.

That pretty much says that trying for
"a cakewalk" by all means, fair or foul,
is just human nature.

Compare the just posted:

http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/msg/16cc3139db3d8c4d?dmode=source

which tells what the game looks like if
the player does _not_ grossly over-prepare.

So, quite possibly, the SporkHack agenda is
fairly misguided, and instead attention to
nerfing the worst of naked AC buildup means,
alchemy overuse, polypiling, and other ways
*deliberately* to _become_ a walking tank
should be the focus.

